      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T12:22:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you\u0027re right. The PPC read here doesn’t add value since it’s only used later in the fallback branch. I’ll move the ppc_is_vbus_present() call inside the else if block so it’s only executed when actually needed",
      "parentUuid": "6dad5163_1dbaf14c",
      "revId": "b67e6978ae5e06f8359bd375dfb99a7b43e2b8a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af86ddd2_7029b330",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/pujjoga/src/usbc.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T00:00:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m suspicious that this offset varies between devices, since the TCPC datasheet specifies 1% accuracy for the ADC: 100 mV is less than 1% of the full-scale VBUS voltage (20V) so there\u0027s no guarantee of this being accurate.",
      "revId": "b67e6978ae5e06f8359bd375dfb99a7b43e2b8a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7090686a_d1072e5f",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/pujjoga/src/usbc.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T15:31:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you concerned that the size of the offset is too small or more generally that a constant offset is too simple to correct this measurement?\n\nIf the former, would a 200 mV or 250 mV offset seem more reasonable to you?",
      "parentUuid": "af86ddd2_7029b330",
      "revId": "b67e6978ae5e06f8359bd375dfb99a7b43e2b8a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91f998d4_f7585b92",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/pujjoga/src/usbc.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-30T00:14:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "100mV may be too small for some devices; 250mV is probably okay since it accounts for the worst-case ADC error, although ideally we\u0027d also account for error introduced by resistor tolerance on the input (since the ADC is fed via a resistive divider).",
      "parentUuid": "7090686a_d1072e5f",
      "revId": "b67e6978ae5e06f8359bd375dfb99a7b43e2b8a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2690be1a_f175fcba",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/pujjoga/src/usbc.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-31T17:00:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For now, if 250 works for pujjoga, I\u0027d say we should merge it.\n\nIdeally, I\u0027d like this offset to live inside the NCT3xxx driver. If we need further offsets based on board resistors, we can keep those in board code. We\u0027ll have to figure that out as we work our way through different models. Right now, I think we\u0027ve only seen this particular failure mode on pujjoga.",
      "parentUuid": "91f998d4_f7585b92",
      "revId": "b67e6978ae5e06f8359bd375dfb99a7b43e2b8a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
